{actorTwo.name} pops around the corner. "What are you two talking about?"

{actorOne.name} whips out a pad, waving it in {actorTwo.name}'s face. {capitalize: actorOne.pronouns.subject} notices you outside of {actorOne.pronouns.dependent} field of vision, and motions you to come closer, to join {actorTwo.name} in an impromptu semi-circle to bear witness. "{actorOneViewing}" {actorTwo.pronouns.subject} says, shaking the pad with vigor. You catch a [[small figure towards the edge of the screen->Theosebeia_Video]].

:: Theosebeia_Video
Debris clouds the screen, rocks sliding into frame to obscure the woman sitting on her grav board. Just as quickly, they pass by; she is the only constant among this field of debris. A broken planet rests in the bottom of the frame, a hole straight through the center pointing back out towards an enormity of stars. The scoreboard is at about a minute and a half left, and counting. Announcers are excitedly sharing details as she hoists herself into an upright standing position. If she can't make a winning play now, she's out, they breathlessly chatter. Theosebeia has been giving upsets this whole game, but a few chokes midway through leaves no room for error. She's got time for one big score, and that's it.

In a flash, so fast you barely notice it, she's diving. Her board accelerates down, engines burning through what remains of the ozone below as the camera tilts to follow. Color commentators are screaming, desperate to understand the world in a moment as Theosebeia rockets towards the planet's core. You try to understand the words pouring out of the mouths of the folks in the sound booths. Surely, pulling 5 Gs down is a huge boon, but will that be enough? Will she wipe out before making the points she needs? A risky gamble, they deride. Theosebeia has been the underdog this whole time, but there's no reason to think that she'll be able to-

She can hear them. A psychic force letting her know how to upset, how to drive these folks wild. There are 30 seconds left on the clock, and Theosebeia is at maximum speed, accelerating as much as her board can handle; according to the overlay she's at about 20 Gs. She's rocketing through, going faster and faster, straight towards the center of the planet. You find yourself holding your breath. Even knowing this is a recording, you feel like any utterance of sound would break history. Would end an otherwise astonishing moment.

The screaming announcers become wailing sirens. Theosebeia has left her board, is gliding at a breakneck pace into a planet without any form of control.